<subpara id="X39400000R101OC_10" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000D3600000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>The intake air flow meter uses a platinum filament. It consists of a heater made of platinum filament, a temperature sensor and a control circuit built into the housing. In operation, the heater in the bypass passage of the housing is cooled by the passing intake air, and the temperature sensor detects that temperature change. In the circuit, the heater and temperature sensor form a bridge circuit, and the action of the power transistor that controls the heater to maintain a set temperature (potential difference between A and B) is measured as the output voltage of the intake air flow meter.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A127143J07" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</item>
</list1>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1" pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<colspec colnum="01" colname="C01" colwidth="0.96in"/>
